      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- TIP_DETAIL\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS\n- SUBJECT_SUMMARY\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\n\n## Column Mapping\n- subject title: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_TITLE, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- department name: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- material count: TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_KEY\n- offering department name: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- responsible faculty name: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME\n- TIP material status key: TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\n- total units: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\n- window column: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.COURSE_NUMBER\n- school name: SIS_DEPARTMENT.SCHOOL_NAME\n- department phone: SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_PHONE_NUMBER\n- top 10 by number of materials: TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_KEY\n- 2014FA term: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- enrolled student: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n\n## Join Keys\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> TIP_DETAIL.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID <-> TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID <-> TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. List the top 10 subject titles by the number of materials offered, including the subject title, department name, and the total count of materials, for subjects in regular academic terms.\n```sql\nSELECT ss.SUBJECT_TITLE, ss.DEPARTMENT_NAME, COUNT(td.TIP_MATERIAL_KEY) AS material_count FROM TIP_DETAIL td JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS at ON td.TERM_CODE = at.TERM_CODE JOIN SUBJECT_SUMMARY ss ON at.TERM_CODE = ss.TERM_CODE AND td.SUBJECT_ID = ss.SUBJECT_ID WHERE at.IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y' GROUP BY ss.SUBJECT_TITLE, ss.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY material_count DESC LIMIT 10;\n```\n2. For all subjects in the 2014FA term with at least one enrolled student, show the subject title, offering department name, responsible faculty name, the TIP material status key, the total number of units, and the minimum total number of units in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the course number.\n```sql\nSELECT lso.SUBJECT_TITLE, lso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, lso.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME, td.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, sos.TOTAL_UNITS, MIN(sos.TOTAL_UNITS) OVER (ORDER BY sos.COURSE_NUMBER ROWS BETWEEN 3 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING) AS window_column FROM LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED lso JOIN TIP_DETAIL td ON lso.SUBJECT_ID = td.SUBJECT_ID JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY sos ON td.SUBJECT_ID = sos.SUBJECT_ID WHERE lso.TERM_CODE = '2014FA' AND lso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0\n```\n3. List all subject titles that are either among the top 10 by number of materials offered in regular academic terms or are subjects in the 2014FA term with at least one enrolled student, and for each include: subject title, department name, total count of materials, offering department name, responsible faculty name, TIP material status key, total number of units, the minimum total number of units in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the course number, and the reason for inclusion ('TopSubjects' for top 10 by materials, 'Subjects2014FA' for 2014FA subjects with enrollment). The columns should be: subject title, department name, material count, offering department name, responsible faculty name, TIP material status key, total units, window column, and reason.\n```sql\nWITH TopSubjects AS ( SELECT ss.SUBJECT_TITLE, ss.DEPARTMENT_NAME, COUNT(td.TIP_MATERIAL_KEY) AS material_count, ss.SUBJECT_ID FROM TIP_DETAIL td JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS at ON td.TERM_CODE = at.TERM_CODE JOIN SUBJECT_SUMMARY ss ON at.TERM_CODE = ss.TERM_CODE AND td.SUBJECT_ID = ss.SUBJECT_ID WHERE at.IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y' GROUP BY ss.SUBJECT_TITLE, ss.DEPARTMENT_NAME, ss.SUBJECT_ID ORDER BY material_count DESC LIMIT 10 ), Subjects2014FA AS ( SELECT lso.SUBJECT_TITLE, lso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, lso.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME, td.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, sos.TOTAL_UNITS, MIN(sos.TOTAL_UNITS) OVER (ORDER BY sos.COURSE_NUMBER ROWS BETWEEN 3 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING) AS window_column, lso.SUBJECT_ID FROM LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED lso JOIN TIP_DETAIL td ON lso.SUBJECT_ID = td.SUBJECT_ID JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY sos ON td.SUBJECT_ID = sos.SUBJECT_ID WHERE lso.TERM_CODE = '2014FA' AND lso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0 ), CombinedSubjects AS ( SELECT ts.SUBJECT_TITLE, ts.DEPARTMENT_NAME, ts.material_count, NULL AS OFFER_DEPT_NAME, NULL AS RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME, NULL AS TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, NULL AS TOTAL_UNITS, NULL AS window_column, 'TopSubjects' AS Reason FROM TopSubjects ts UNION ALL SELECT s2014.SUBJECT_TITLE, NULL AS DEPARTMENT_NAME, NULL AS material_count, s2014.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, s2014.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME, s2014.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, s2014.TOTAL_UNITS, s2014.window_column, 'Subjects2014FA' AS Reason FROM Subjects2014FA s2014 ) SELECT * FROM CombinedSubjects ORDER BY SUBJECT_TITLE;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each subject that is either among the top 10 by number of materials offered in regular academic terms or is a subject in the 2014FA term with at least one enrolled student, list the subject title, department name, total count of materials, offering department name, responsible faculty name, TIP material status key, total number of units, the minimum total number of units in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the course number, the school name, and the department phone number. Also, include the reason for inclusion ('TopSubjects' for top 10 by materials, 'Subjects2014FA' for 2014FA subjects with enrollment). The columns should be: subject title, department name, material count, offering department name, responsible faculty name, TIP material status key, total units, window column, school name, department phone, and reason. Do not return any rounded answers."
